            ("Examples", ["Removing paint, anodizing, or oxide while attempting to preserve the substrate is selective ablation. Engraving depth into metal uses repeated overlapping ablation events. Laser cleaning removes contamination or corrosion when the unwanted layer responds more strongly than the base material. Fine drilling and micromachining remove successive volumes with tightly controlled pulses.", "A dark annealed stainless-steel mark is mainly a thermal or chemical surface modification rather than deep ablation. Cutting usually combines removal with melting, vaporization, assist gas, and material separation, so it is broader than ablation alone."]),
